          "worked_solution": "Since we have a repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ (of multiplicity two) and only one corresponding eigenvector $v,$ the solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}v{e}^{\\lambda t}+{c}_{2}(vt{e}^{\\lambda t}+w{e}^{\\lambda t}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ is a solution to the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$\n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n\\lambda =2,\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nThus, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}] & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{2t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x\\text{-axis}.$ Since ${e}^{2t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions move toward $\\text{infinity}$ in the phase plane as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14150888/assets/98fc60d566b520f3d943e42ee8f4e07aa0bdd33b53fbb04981c2e8f4001210fd.png)\n\nNow, consider solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\nWhen ${c}_{2}=1,$ we get the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=t{e}^{2t} \\\\ y={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $-0.5$ | $0$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-0.18$ | $0$ | $1.36$ |\n| $y$ | $0.37$ | $1$ | $2.72$ |\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14150888/assets/2f56bfb6777e6d95dfd887a525ea69a58725fc4f1a81bea84ebde67a72812518.png)\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14150888/assets/2c9158f2818c1630debba65361b9be35a583d74591e389728528ffc3409ed89b.png)",
